  "live_records": {
    "q-96575": {
      "dom_id": "step-q96575",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "The discrete random variable $X\\in Z$ can be approximated by the continuous random variable $Y.$ By applying an appropriate continuity correction, $P(X=-6)$ can be approximated as",
      "worked_solution": "We construct an interval around $X=-6$ with a radius of $0.5:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14128539/assets/9f21d7fe3ba1f4efa7b4e24e3d096d84825ff3712f5854c76dabccf0477f503c.png)\n\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=-6) & ≈P(-6-0.5\\le Y\\le -6+0.5) \\\\  & =P(-6.5\\le Y\\le -5.5).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
