    "q-96643": {
      "dom_id": "step-q96643",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "The discrete random variable $X\\in Z$ can be approximated by the continuous random variable $Y.$ By applying an appropriate continuity correction, $P(2<X<7)$ can be approximated as",
      "worked_solution": "To apply the appropriate continuity correction, we first rewrite the strict inequalities as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2<X<7) & =P(3\\le X\\le 6)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we extend the endpoints of the interval $3\\le X\\le 6$ by $0.5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(3\\le X\\le 6) & ≈P(3-0.5\\le Y\\le 6+0.5) \\\\  & =P(2.5\\le Y\\le 6.5)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
