    "q-132239": {
      "dom_id": "step-q132239",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "The discrete random variable $X\\in Z$ can be approximated by the continuous random variable $Y.$ By applying an appropriate continuity correction, $P(X>19)$ can be approximated as",
      "worked_solution": "To apply the appropriate continuity correction, we first rewrite the strict inequality as follows:\n\n$$\nP(X>19)=P(X\\ge 20)\n$$\n\nThen, we extend the endpoints of the interval $X\\ge 20$ by $0.5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 20) & ≈P(Y\\ge 20-0.5) \\\\  & =P(Y\\ge 19.5)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
